<speak>For an appointment message, keeping it brief and administrative is a good approach. It can identify who contacted you and invite you to use the bank's usual contact route to arrange a suitable time, without including private details. If you receive something you're unsure about, you can use a contact channel you already know rather than relying on unfamiliar links. We can keep the scheduling conversation separate from any substantive discussion, so an appointment reminder doesn't turn into another long task for you.</speak>